  <content>
    <section>
      <title>Activity</title>
      <note class="link-to-learning">
      <para>Access the <link
          url="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/b62c9150250bf52d6cc37569213ab516e0090dca">Desmos
        guide PDF</link> for tips on solving problems with the Desmos graphing calculator.</para>
        </note>

      <para>Below are three systems of equations you saw earlier.</para>
      <para>Use System A to answer questions 1 – 6.</para>
      <para>System A</para>
      <para>\(\left\{\begin{array}{c}4x+3y=10\;\\-4x+5y=6\end{array}\right.\)</para>
      <!--Q#1-->

      
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <!--QUESTION
          IS OUTSIDE OF INTERACTION DUE TO DESMOS-->
          <para>Use the graphing tool or technology outside the course. Graph the equations for System
            A that represent this scenario using the Desmos tool below.</para>
        <media alt="">
        <iframe src="../../media/desmos/a47b5bb4ba783be55a7067b919f165f14dcc36ce.html" width="500"
          height="400" />
        </media>
          <para>When you have finished graphing, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis>
            button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <figure class="unnumbered">
            <media alt="Insert Alt Text">
              <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_06_06_01.png" />
            </media>
          
        </solution>
      </exercise>

      <!--Interaction
      End -->

        <exercise id="_4da44566-324d-4927-8c3f-81dbeb4e1863" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>

            <para>Identify the \(x\) coordinate of the solution.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! The answer is 1.</para>
            <para>The answer is 1.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>

        <exercise id="efc3fc12-dbd8-4bf8-9e76-6c35c06b71c5" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Identify the \(y\) coordinate of the solution.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! The answer is 1.</para>
            <para>The answer is 1.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>


      <!--Q#4-->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Find the sum or difference of the two original equations that would enable the
            system to be solved.</para>

        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>Your answer may vary, but here are some samples.</para>
          <list>
            <item>Sample Answer 1: \(8y=16 \)</item>
            <item>Sample Answer 2: \(y=2 \)</item>
            <item>Sample Answer 3: \(8x−2y=4 \)</item>
          </list>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction
      End -->
